 "intuition": "A thin lens is two refracting surfaces with nothing between them, so the image formed by the first is the object of the second and the two powers simply add: $P=P_1+P_2$. The result depends on $n$, $R_1$, $R_2$ only, which is why a lens can be designed on paper.",
